Well, I've participated in the "shoes" debate and now in the "bathtub"
debate, though I stayed out of the "mescaline I have known and loved"
discussion.

To put it bluntly, with that caveat in mind, I think the quality of
debate on Extropians is seriously declining. I attribute this to the
loss of key "idea" people like Tom Morrow, Hal Finney, Robin Hanson,
and some others. And (apparently) remaining list members like Perry
Metzger and Dean Tribble are being oftly quiet lately. (Though some
idea people like Charlie Stross have returned, and I won't list the
_ongoing_ idea people who remain, of which there are many.)

Perhaps we've hit the main topics. I don't know. What I know is that
discussions often evolve into chit-chat about personal tastes and
preferences....in fact, it's about time now for the usual discussion
about "Extropian music," isn't it?

Our "virtual seminars" seem to typically get 3-5 people involved,
which isn't much. (Nick Szabo and I are discussing starting one on
virtual worlds, business enterprises in VR, MOOs and MUDs, etc.)

I _really_ wonder what the 250 or so people who rarely post are
getting out of the List. Will any of them comment?

Don't take my remarks too negatively. Maybe the List is just going
through a lull, maybe I just need to unsubscribe for a while and come
back reinvigorated.

In any case, Kennita asked and I have answered.


